# opt-nout-same-line: nout=2 and then njmp=4 in the same @ list, which one wins (XPPAUT 8.2.2)?
# xpp: rows=3
# pc: ok
# ruling: matches: nout and njmp set one value, so the last entry wins, also inside one @ list (crates/pc-ode/docs/language.md, Lists)
x'=1
x(0)=0
aux v=x
@ total=4,dt=0.5,meth=euler,nout=2,njmp=4
